{"id": "unknown-2026-07-27-032", "date": "2026-07-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 31, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["improve", "uncertainty"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "New disaggregation methodology quantifies uncertainty in behind-the-meter PV generation", "content": "<p>Researchers in Spain have developed a conditional diffusion-based model to improve the visibility of behind-the-meter PV systems using low-resolution smart meter data. The probabilistic approach enables accurate PV reconstruction with uncertainty estimates, helping distribution system operators better manage grid planning and flexibility.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/27/new-disaggregation-methodology-quantifies-uncertainty-in-behind-the-meter-pv-generation-and-", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/27/new-disaggregation-methodology-quantifies-uncertainty-in-behind-the-meter-pv-generation-and-heat-pump-demand/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-27-033", "date": "2026-07-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 31, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s Advait Greenergy, China’s GuofuHee showcase 5 MW alkaline electrolyzer", "content": "<p>The live demonstration brought together more than 70 organizations from across the green hydrogen value chain, giving participants an opportunity to evaluate the electrolyzer under real operating conditions.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/27/advait-greenergy-guofuhee-showcase-5-mw-alkaline-electrolyser-in-live-factory-acceptance-testing-ahead-of-india-deployment/\">India&#8217;s Advait Greenergy, China&#8217;s GuofuHee showcase 5 MW alkaline electrolyzer</a> appea", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/27/advait-greenergy-guofuhee-showcase-5-mw-alkaline-electrolyser-in-live-factory-acceptance-testing-ahead-of-india-deployment/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-27-034", "date": "2026-07-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 31, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Canadian Solar subsidiary opens 6 GW solar cell factory in Indiana", "content": "<p>Canadian Solar subsidiary CS PowerTech officially opened phase one of its solar cell manufacturing plant in Jeffersonville, Indiana, targeting over 6 GW of annual capacity at full buildout.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/27/canadian-solar-subsidiary-opens-6-gw-solar-cell-factory-in-indiana/\">Canadian Solar subsidiary opens 6 GW solar cell factory in Indiana</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/27/canadian-solar-subsidiary-opens-6-gw-solar-cell-factory-in-indiana/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-27-035", "date": "2026-07-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 31, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Three-year testing assesses wind flow dynamics in solar plants", "content": "<p>A French research team analyzed nearly three years of wind and turbulence measurements over a 140-hectare photovoltaic park in southwestern France, comparing it with a nearby pine forest to understand airflow behavior above PV canopies. They found that wind direction relative to panel rows strongly controls turbulence and drag, and they developed a generalized wind-profile parameterization to better represent PV parks in land–atmosphere and weather models.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/27/three-year-testing-assesses-wind-flow-dynamics-in-solar-plants/", "type": "rss"}]}
